<task id="001" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Phase-0 audit (spike): live `sprk_communicationthread`/`sprk_communication` schema; confirm category/tags absent (Q2); verify email-r4 `Services/Communication` merged state; plan `sprk_role` choice-integers</title>
    <phase>W0 — Schema + Foundation + ADR</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <blocks>002, 003</blocks>
    <tags>dataverse, spike</tags>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Read-only Phase-0 verification spike — no schema mutation, no BFF code, no Step 9.5 gates. STANDARD per §8 (spike/inventory with a constraint set). It grounds the two schema deltas (002/003) so they add exactly what is missing; getting the live column delta + `sprk_role` integer plan wrong here cascades into wrong schema, so it is not MINIMAL.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W0-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>— (Phase-0 spike; grounds FR-06 + FR-08)</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    De-risk the two W0 schema deltas (002 `sprk_communicationthread` typed-regarding lookups + markers; 003 `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction) by confirming the CURRENT live state before anything is added. This is a read-only spike — NO schema change, NO code change. Produce ONE findings note under `projects/messaging-communication-app-r2/notes/` that 002 and 003 consume so they add exactly what is missing (never recreate an existing column).

    Confirm, at minimum, using Dataverse MCP against the live env:

    1. **Live `sprk_communicationthread` schema** — enumerate its current attributes. Confirm the as-built set from `notes/messaging-schema-spec.md` (R1): `sprk_name`, `sprk_threadtype`, `sprk_privacystate`, `sprk_privacyeffectivefrom`, denormalized regarding TEXT quartet incl. `sprk_regardingrecordtype` (**Text**). Confirm there are **NO typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups yet**, **NO Lookup discriminator**, **NO naming-edited marker**, and **NO default-thread marker** — i.e. exactly what task 002 must add.
    2. **Q2 negative check** — confirm **category / tags / description are ABSENT** on the thread (spec drops them from CC-1; the schema pass must NOT add them).
    3. **Live `sprk_communication` schema** — confirm the fields the participant write + reads depend on exist: `sprk_communicationtype` (channel choice), `sprk_sentby`, `sprk_sentat`, `sprk_regardingperson`, the `sprk_from`/`sprk_to`/`sprk_cc` TEXT fields, `sprk_cc`/`sprk_bcc`, and that **NO `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction exists yet** (task 003 creates it net-new).
    4. **email-r4 `Services/Communication` merged state on THIS worktree** — grep-verify the key R1/email-r4 files are present (this worktree is synced to master, but confirm empirically): `Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs`, `Services/Communication/ThreadResolver.cs`, `Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/ParticipantCorrelationRung.cs`, `Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs`, `Services/Communication/Models/ParticipantReference.cs`. Note the `RegardingFieldMap.All` 11-entity → typed-lookup-field list verbatim (002 mirrors it).
    5. **`sprk_role` choice-integer plan** — inspect existing Spaarke Choice/optionset integer conventions (via MCP `describe` on an existing option set, e.g. `sprk_communicationtype`) and PROPOSE the exact integer values task 003 will assign to `sprk_role` {From, To, Cc, Bcc} (e.g. the `100000000`+ base). This is a mechanical plan, not a decision — record it so 003 assigns deterministically.

    Do NOT mutate schema, do NOT write code. The single deliverable is the findings note (the confirmed column delta + the `RegardingFieldMap.All` list + the `sprk_role` integer plan).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema-verification engineer. Fluent in the Dataverse MCP read tools (`describe`, `read_query`, `search`), Spaarke option-set integer conventions, and the `Services/Communication/**` layout shipped by R1 / email-r4. You confirm ground truth and hand the next two schema tasks an exact, do-not-recreate delta — you add nothing speculative and change nothing live.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A findings note exists under `projects/messaging-communication-app-r2/notes/` recording: (a) the live `sprk_communicationthread` attribute set with the confirmed ABSENCE of typed regarding lookups / Lookup discriminator / naming-edited marker / default-thread marker (the exact 002 delta) and of category/tags/description (Q2); (b) the live `sprk_communication` attribute set confirming the read/participant dependencies exist and NO participant junction exists yet (the 003 net-new confirmation); (c) grep-confirmation that the five email-r4/R1 `Services/Communication` reference files are present on this worktree plus the verbatim `RegardingFieldMap.All` list; (d) the proposed `sprk_role` {From,To,Cc,Bcc} choice-integer plan. 002 and 003 can build against ground truth with no re-creation risk. No schema or code changed.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R2 is mostly read-surface + UI over R1's data model plus two schema deltas (design §Executive Summary). The two deltas (002 thread lookups/markers, 003 participant junction) must be ADDITIVE and non-breaking (NFR-04). The one recurring failure mode in Dataverse schema work is recreating a column that already exists, or retyping a field that must stay (the Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` — retyping it is breaking, spec §Out-of-Scope). This spike removes that risk by pinning the live delta before any create call.

      The R1 investigation already surfaced the key facts this spike CONFIRMS live: thread `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is **Text** (not Lookup) so RegardingResolver needs a NEW Lookup discriminator; participant data is unqueryable today (`sprk_from/to/cc` are `;`-joined TEXT, no junction). See `notes/r2-resource-investigation.md` §1/§5 and `../messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/messaging-schema-spec.md`. This task verifies those against the live env rather than trusting the note, and produces the integer plan the note does not contain.

      This is a spike (verify-before-build, design §Phase 0), not new surface — no §11 Component Justification is required (it introduces no component; it changes nothing).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r2/notes/r2-resource-investigation.md (§1 regarding/thread model + §5 membership/person — the audit this spike confirms live)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/messaging-schema-spec.md (R1 as-built thread/communication schema — confirm live)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r2/spec.md (FR-06, FR-08, Q2, NFR-04 — what 002/003 must add / must not touch)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs (the 11-entity → typed-lookup map 002 mirrors — capture `All` verbatim)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">READ-ONLY. This spike MUST NOT create, update, or delete any Dataverse attribute/entity/option-set and MUST NOT modify any code. The single deliverable is a findings note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-04 / Out-of-Scope">Confirm the thread's `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is **Text** and flag it as MUST-NOT-RETYPE; the 002 delta is a NEW Lookup discriminator, never a retype of this field.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec Q2">Confirm category / tags / description are ABSENT on `sprk_communicationthread`; the note MUST record that 002/003 do NOT add them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Use Dataverse MCP read tools (`describe`/`read_query`/`search`) for live schema; verify option-set integer conventions via MCP before proposing `sprk_role` values. Do NOT guess integers from memory.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Grep-verify (empirically, not by trusting the sync claim) that the five `Services/Communication/**` reference files are present on this worktree; record the `RegardingFieldMap.All` 11-entity list verbatim for 002.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Blocks 002 + 003 — the note MUST be specific enough that each adds exactly the missing columns with zero re-creation and a deterministic `sprk_role` integer assignment.</constraint>
  </constraints>

