  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The findings note enumerates the live `sprk_communicationthread` attributes and confirms the ABSENCE of typed regarding lookups, a Lookup discriminator, a naming-edited marker, and a default-thread marker (the exact 002 delta).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note confirms `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is **Text** and flags it MUST-NOT-RETYPE (NFR-04); and confirms category/tags/description are ABSENT (Q2) and are not to be added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note enumerates the live `sprk_communication` attributes needed by the reads/participant write and confirms NO `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction exists yet (003 is net-new).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note records grep-confirmation that all five `Services/Communication/**` reference files are present on this worktree and includes the verbatim `RegardingFieldMap.All` 11-entity list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note proposes deterministic, convention-aligned `sprk_role` {From, To, Cc, Bcc} choice-integer values (verified against an existing option set via MCP), ready for 003 to assign.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: no Dataverse attribute/entity/option-set was created, updated, or deleted, and no source code was modified — this task changed nothing live (read-only spike).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Blocks 002 (thread typed-regarding lookups + markers) and 003 (participant junction). Both consume this note's delta so they add ONLY what is missing — the whole point of Phase 0 is to prevent re-creating existing columns and to prevent retyping the Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype`.

    The `sprk_role` integer plan is a mechanical detail (spec Unresolved Questions marks it as the one residual, not a decision) — pin it here so 003 is deterministic.

    Do NOT skip the live MCP read in favor of trusting the R1 note — the note is the hypothesis; this task confirms it against the deployed env.
  </notes>

